# Copy this file to `.env` in the project directory, then fill in at least one key.
#
#   Linux/macOS   cp .env.example .env
#   Windows       copy .env.example .env        (PowerShell: Copy-Item .env.example .env)
#
# `.env` is gitignored — this file holds a credential that spends your money, so it
# never gets committed and never gets pasted into a terminal screenshot.
#
# A key is needed only for `score-job`, `rank`, `tailor` and `record-fixtures`. `collect`,
# `jobs`, `ats`, `closing` and `start-here` run without one.
#
# EVERY key below is a free tier that needs no credit card. The tool tries them in this
# order and silently skips the ones you did not fill in, so one key works and four keys
# give you a deeper daily budget. They are all pinned for structured JSON output; the
# model ids live in config.py MODEL_CHAIN.

# Hop 1 — fastest, and the default. Free tier at console.groq.com. NOTE: its limit is
# tokens PER DAY (~200,000 on gpt-oss-120b), so `rank`/`tailor` stop once today's
# window is spent unless a second key below is set.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Hop 2 — Google AI Studio (aistudio.google.com), generous free quota. The single most
# useful second key: it is the difference between "come back tomorrow" and working now.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Hop 3 — cerebras.ai. Free tier is a large daily token budget (1M/day reported on
# Llama-4 Scout and Qwen3 32B). Model id taken from their public docs, not yet exercised
# from a real key here.
CEREBRAS_API_KEY=

# Hop 4 — openrouter.ai. One key, many `:free` models behind an OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
# Model pinned to one that declares structured_outputs in OpenRouter's own public list.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Real model calls are opt-in and off by default, so that tests and CI can never
# spend money by accident. Without this line the tool replays recorded answers and
# refuses to invent one for a prompt it has never seen.
CAREERPILOT_LIVE=1
